    "q-162949": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162949",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14120744/assets/d64311921135cf8dea0ec70bb0a83909fb1dba52664f4d6080de596be1693d5e.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+2\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+2,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot ({x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}+2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}+{2}^{2})-(\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4}+{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4} \\\\  & =6.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $6.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
